    "turn_text": "news. You'll hear it first on KSL News Radio. When the news out of Washington DC has been interesting, you look at the transition of power, especially in the Senate. You look at leadership now has been voted on and is in place. You look at those who have been sworn in today. You look at Utah's incredible prominence in the 114th Congress, not to mention other areas, too, with our Salt Lake City Mayor Ralph Becker. You look at the governor who's back in Washington, D.C. Today, as a matter of fact, momentarily, if not now, he'll be meeting with the president, and he spoke to the National Governors Association as its vice chair and delivered the state of the states address you look at our state senator bramble his prominent role with state legislators from around the country and then the new leadership positions that we have from our delegation the committee chairmanship the committees that they are serving on and then we get this word that Mitch McConnell has named senator mike lee as Council to the Senate Majority Leader, and we have Senator Lee on the line with us. First of all, Senator Lee, my congratulations.",
