  {
    "episode_id": 64503,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/6/4/64503.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 12,
    "turn_text": "Well, I'm the incoming chairman of the Senate Steering Committee, and I think it made sense to him to bring the chairman of the Steering Committee into his leadership meeting, and I think that might have a lot to do with why I was brought in there. But yeah, in a broader sense, I think this was an effort on his part to try to unite the Senate Republican Conference and to get different perspectives regionally and ideologically into the same room. And to help ease some of the tension between the base that exists within any political party and the establishment within any political party, including our own. And I think I can help him with that. And I look forward to working with him on that.",
